  "Number": 16,
  "Question": "If the base of a rectangle is increased by \\(10\\%\\) and the area is unchanged, then the altitude is decreased by:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\dfrac19\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\dfrac1{11}\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "A rectangle's area is base times altitude. Since the area stays fixed, multiplying its positive base by a factor requires dividing the altitude by that factor.\n\nThe new base is \\(110\\%=\\frac{11}{10}\\) of the original, so the new altitude is \\(\\frac{10}{11}\\) of the original. The fraction lost is therefore\n\\[\n1-\\frac{10}{11}=\\frac1{11}.\n\\]\nAs a percentage of the original altitude, this is\n\\[\n\\frac1{11}\\cdot100\\%=\\frac{100}{11}\\%=9\\frac1{11}\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
